## 7. Phase 4 — Consumer migration (target: 1–2 weeks per consumer, parallelizable)

### 7a. RankEvolve — Python migration first, then React

RE is the **most invasive** consumer because of its parallel Python
fork. Do Python before React so the React side has a coherent backend.

#### 7a.1 Replace Python imports

In RE, change every:
```python
from rankevolve.src.agentic_foundation.common.ui.X import Y
```
to:
```python
from agent_foundation.ui import Y
```

The aliases land in Phase 0's `__init__.py` barrel so most imports
become single-line.

#### 7a.2 Adjust for the `MULTIPLE_CHOICES` plural

RE uses `InputMode.MULTIPLE_CHOICES` in conditionals. The cleanest
migration is a one-line `sed`:
```bash
git grep -l "InputMode\.MULTIPLE_CHOICES" rankevolve/src/ | xargs sed -i '' 's/InputMode\.MULTIPLE_CHOICES/InputMode.MULTIPLE_CHOICE/g'
```
The Phase-0 alias in `input_modes.from_dict` keeps the wire format working
for any backwards-compat consumer.

#### 7a.3 Delete the RE Python fork

Delete these files from `rankevolve/src/agentic_foundation/common/ui/`:
- `widget_protocol.py`
- `input_modes.py`
- `interactive_base.py`
- `rich_interactive_base.py`
- `queue_interactive.py`
- `interactive_checkpoint.py`
- `terminal_interactive.py`
- `web_interactive.py`

Keep:
- `proposal_models.py`, `proposal_parser.py`, `learnings_parser.py`
  (RE-specific domain models — out of scope for this plan).

#### 7a.4 Adjust the Debuggable decoupling

If Phase 0 chose to drop `Debuggable` from `WebUIInteractive` (option a),
adjust RE's WebSocket handler to instantiate `WebUIInteractive` without
Debuggable. If Phase 0 chose to create `agent_foundation.utils.debuggable`
(option b), RE imports that instead.

#### 7a.5 React migration for RE

Add to `rankevolve/src/webui/react/package.json`:
```json
"dependencies": {
  "@agent-foundation/shared-ui": "0.1.0"
}
```
…installed from Atlassian Artifactory.

Then replace imports per the classification matrix (Section 9). Keep
local: `ProposalSelectionWidget`, `MultiViewTaskPanel`,
`PipelineStatusBar`, `components/hub/*`, `components/views/*`. Register
them via `registerWidget('rankevolve.proposal_selection', …)`.

#### 7a.6 RE exit criteria

- `pytest` green in RE.
- `from agent_foundation.ui import WebUIInteractive` works inside RE.
- `npm run start` for the React app: demo mode + real (WebSocket) mode
  both work; widgets render; snapshot diff against pre-migration
  baseline is zero or explicitly approved.
- No files remain under `rankevolve/src/agentic_foundation/common/ui/`
  except `proposal_models.py`, `proposal_parser.py`, `learnings_parser.py`.

### 7b. OpenStartup — React migration

OS does not have a Python fork to migrate; only React.

#### 7b.1 Add the dependency

```diff
"dependencies": {
+  "@agent-foundation/shared-ui": "0.1.0",
   "@mui/material": "^7.3.9",
   ...
}
```

For local development, the relative path option works when both repos
are checked out under `CoreProjects/`:
```diff
+  "@agent-foundation/shared-ui": "file:../../AgentFoundation/src/agent_foundation/ui/react-shared",
```
Documented in `react-shared/README.md` as the preferred dev-loop.

#### 7b.2 Replace `shared/`

`openteam/ui/src/shared/index.js` becomes:
```js
export {
  EmptyState, LoadingIndicator, PersonChip, ProgressBar,
  QuickLinkButton, SectionCard, StatusBadge,
} from '@agent-foundation/shared-ui';
export { default as PendingReasonPopover } from './PendingReasonPopover';
```
Delete the seven individual `shared/*.js` files (keep
`PendingReasonPopover` locally until Phase 3 generalizes it; then
re-export from library).

#### 7b.3 Replace chat-widgets

- Re-export `TextInputWidget`, `SingleChoiceWidget`,
  `MultipleChoiceWidget`, `ConfirmationWidget`, `ApprovalWidget`,
  `ChoiceWidget`, `ChatWidgetRenderer`, `ConversationToolWidget`,
  `WidgetRegistry` from library.
- Keep `ProjectSummaryWidget`, `SprintProgressWidget`,
  `TaskAssignmentWidget`, `TaskListWidget`, `WorkloadChartWidget`
  local. At app bootstrap call:
  ```js
  registerWidget('openteam.project_summary', ProjectSummaryWidget);
  registerWidget('openteam.sprint_progress', SprintProgressWidget);
  registerWidget('openteam.task_assignment', TaskAssignmentWidget);
  registerWidget('openteam.task_list', TaskListWidget);
  registerWidget('openteam.workload_chart', WorkloadChartWidget);
  ```

#### 7b.4 Replace theme

`openteam/ui/src/theme/` becomes a one-file re-export shim plus any
OpenTEAM-flavored theme overrides:
```js
export {
  AppThemeProvider, ThemeSwitcher, themeRegistry, createAppTheme,
} from '@agent-foundation/shared-ui/theme';
// OS-specific theme add-on:
import { registerTheme } from '@agent-foundation/shared-ui/theme';
import openstartupTheme from './themes/openstartup';
registerTheme('openstartup', openstartupTheme);
```

#### 7b.5 Replace chat/* generics

Replace `chat/MarkdownRenderer.js`, `chat/StreamingMessage.js`,
`chat/Breadcrumb.js`, `chat/CommandAutocomplete.js`,
`chat/PromptViewerDrawer.js`, `chat/ThinkingFold.js`,
`chat/AgentMessageBubble.js`, `chat/GraphFlowView.js`,
`chat/NodeDetailPanel.js` with library re-exports.

Keep local: `SessionContextBar`, `TaskCard`, `TaskPanel`,
`BackendSelector` (until Phase 3 extracts ModelSelector primitive).

#### 7b.6 OS exit criteria

- `npm install && npm run start` works.
- All views render visually unchanged (screenshot diff baseline gated).
- `grep -rE "from '.*shared/(EmptyState|LoadingIndicator|PersonChip|ProgressBar|QuickLinkButton|SectionCard|StatusBadge)'" openteam/ui/src/` returns **0** matches outside the re-export shim.
- `grep -rE "from '.*chat-widgets/(TextInput|SingleChoice|MultipleChoice|Confirmation|Approval|Choice)Widget'" openteam/ui/src/` returns **0** matches outside re-export shims.

### 7c. AgentFoundation demo app

Final cleanup:

- Reduce `webui/react/src/components/widgets/`,
  `components/common/`, etc. to **re-export shims only** (or delete the
  directories entirely if no external code imports from them).
- Delete the legacy `webui/src/` tree (dead duplicate of
  `webui/react/src/`).
- Ensure `webui/react/src/components/widgets/index.js` does not silently
  miss any export (the `MultiInputWidget` omission is now moot since
  imports come from the library).
- `webui/backend/main.py` continues to serve unchanged.

