## 8. Phase 5 — Governance & anti-drift (ongoing)

The single biggest **cause** of the current mess is "copy, fork, drift,
copy back." Phase 5 makes that mechanically impossible.

### 8.1 CI guardrails (AgentFoundation repo)

| Check | Script | Fails when |
|-------|--------|------------|
| Python ↔ JS sync | `python react-shared/scripts/sync_widget_types.py --check` | `widget_protocol.py` was edited without regenerating `widgetTypes.js`. |
| Registry completeness | `vitest run tests/registry_completeness.test.js` | A `WIDGET_TYPES` member has no registered component. |
| No duplicate components | `python scripts/check_no_duplicate_widgets.py` | A file in `webui/react/src/components/{widgets,common}/` is not a one-line re-export of the same-named file in `react-shared/src/`. |
| Round-trip protocol | `pytest test/agent_foundation/ui/test_widget_protocol_roundtrip.py` | Wire format breaks. |
| Codeowners on contract files | GitHub native | Anyone tries to edit `widget_protocol.py`/`input_modes.py` without UI-team review. |
| `dist/` rebuilt | `npm run build:check` | `react-shared/dist/` is stale. |

### 8.2 CI guardrails (OpenStartup + RankEvolve repos)

A small `check_no_local_widget_duplicates.py` script (~50 lines) walks
each repo and fails the build if any file in the local
`{chat-widgets,shared,components/common,components/widgets}/` directories
duplicates a name from the library's published manifest. The manifest
is hosted at `https://artifactory.../shared-ui/manifest.json` and
checked at CI time.

### 8.3 `react-shared/CONTRIBUTING.md` (rules)

1. Every new widget MUST add a constant to `widget_protocol.py` first.
2. The PR that adds the widget MUST regenerate `widgetTypes.js` via
   `npm run sync`.
3. The PR MUST add the widget to `registerBuiltins.js`.
4. The PR MUST add a Storybook story.
5. The PR MUST add a Vitest snapshot test.
6. The PR MUST conform to Contract 2 (`{ widget, onSubmit, ... }`).
7. Domain widgets MUST use `namespace.type` and live in the consuming
   app, not in `react-shared/`.

### 8.4 Versioning

- Semver. `0.1.0` is the first cut after Phase 2.
- `0.2.0` removes the `legacyAdapter.js` shim.
- `1.0.0` once both OS and RE have run a full release cycle on `0.x`
  without compatibility shims.
- Breaking changes require a `BREAKING.md` entry in the changeset.

### 8.5 Quarterly drift audit

Cron CI job runs `diff -rq react-shared/src/ <consumer>/src/.../widgets/`
across all three consumers. Any unexpected file (i.e., not a one-line
re-export) opens a tracking ticket automatically via the Jira MCP.

