## 10. Risks & mitigations (deduped, evidence-backed)

| # | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|------|------------|--------|------------|
| R1 | Async base-class change breaks RE's `WebUIInteractive` override | LOW | HIGH | Phase 0 wrappers are non-virtual signatures; RE's override matches them. Add test that exercises both paths. |
| R2 | `Debuggable` decoupling breaks RE's `__repr__` debugging | LOW | LOW | Option (b) — keep a minimal `agent_foundation.utils.debuggable` — preserves behavior. |
| R3 | MUI 7 (OS) vs MUI 5 (AF/RE) symbol divergence | MEDIUM | MEDIUM | `peerDependency >=5 <8`; `ThemeProvider.createThemeFn` prop is **verified** to support both. CI tests against MUI 5 *and* MUI 7. |
| R4 | CRA does not transpile `node_modules` | HIGH (would-be) | HIGH | **Decision: ship pre-built CJS+ESM via `tsup`.** Avoids the `craco` swap for every consumer. |
| R5 | `theme.custom.surfaces.*` bare access crashes on themes without `custom` | HIGH (already happens) | MEDIUM | Phase 1 (§4.5) mandates optional-chaining rewrite. |
| R6 | OS's `chat-widgets/SingleChoiceWidget.js` double-submit guard lost during promotion | MEDIUM | MEDIUM | Phase 2 (§5.2) explicitly names OS as source-of-truth and adds a test that asserts double-submit is no-op. |
| R7 | Python↔JS widget-type drift returns | MEDIUM | HIGH | Codegen + CI `--check` guard (Phase 2 §5.1 + Phase 5 §8.1). |
| R8 | Big-bang migrations cause merge conflicts in active dev | MEDIUM | MEDIUM | Phases are per-bucket PRs; can stop after any and ship. |
| R9 | OS uses React 19; AF/RE use React 18 | LOW | MEDIUM | `peerDependency react>=18`; CI tests both. |
| R10 | Artifactory publishing pipeline doesn't exist in AF | MEDIUM | MEDIUM | Phase 1 sets up `tsup`; Phase 5 sets up publish job. Interim consumption via `npm pack` tarball. |
| R11 | `ConversationToolWidget` ACLI/`<Response>` parsing leaks into generic dispatcher | HIGH | MEDIUM | Phase 2 (§5.2) extracts as `parser` prop (default = identity). |
| R12 | RE's React fork is more up-to-date than AF's in some files | HIGH | LOW | Section 1 verified ground-truth dictates per-file source. `DECISIONS.md` log records choice. |
| R13 | `interactive_checkpoint.py` async bug bites a downstream user during Phase 0 | LOW | HIGH | Phase 0 fixes it in the first commit and adds a regression test. |
| R14 | `MULTIPLE_CHOICES` plural alias confuses new developers | LOW | LOW | Documented in `input_modes.py` docstring + linter rule that warns on new uses. |
| R15 | OpenStartup `shared/PendingReasonPopover.js` references resolution shapes that don't generalize cleanly | MEDIUM | LOW | Phase 3 lifts it as a primitive only after one release of soak time. |

